	abstract = {This study compares the discursive construction of identity in the academic discourse of soft and hard disciplines through the observation of self-mention WE. Based on Sinclair’s (2003) extended unit of meaning, the study scrutinizes the features of WE including collocation, colligation, semantic preference, and semantic prosody in 720 research articles spanning 2018-2022. The findings reveal that the disciplinary differences are reflected in WE in not only the frequency (p{\textless}0.001) but also collocations and further manifested in grammatical structure, semantic meaning, and pragmatic implication. These differences demonstrate that scholars in soft disciplines are more confident while hard are relatively conservative. This study seeks to enhance the understanding of self-mention in the academic discourse of different academic fields, providing insights into English for Specific Purposes in both writing and teaching.},
